    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Stewards can now reopen a closed period, and all 4 acceptance tests pass with `bin/e2e`.\n\n**How it behaves:**\n- Each period row has a new **Reopen** button (`data-testid=\"period-reopen\"`).\n- If anyone other than a steward presses it, the period shows an error (\"Only a steward can reopen a period.\") and nothing is saved. Reopening a period that is already open is also refused with an error (\"That period is not closed.\").\n- On success, the period is marked open and its fixed total is cleared, so its due-total is live again. Claims already show their current figures, with bound ones at their bound figure, so the period total now matches them (6.00 \u2192 11.00 in the test).\n- It writes `PERIOD_REOPENED sheet=<id> by=<user> period=<name>` to the audit file.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **Server:** a new `POST /api/sheets/{sheetId}/periods/{id}/reopen` endpoint in `PeriodController`, `PeriodService.reopen`, and `Period.reopen()`. The service locks the sheet the same way `close` does and checks the role through `SettingService.roleOf`.\n- **Front end:** a `reopen` call in `periods-api.ts`, plus the button and its handler in `periods.ts`. The parent already swaps in the updated period, so the row refreshes without other changes.\n- **Database:** no migration was needed; the existing `closed` and `closed_total` columns are enough.",
